s://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:44:54-08:00","id":841574,"title":"","content":"A thought just occurred to me. Did they keep the same look of the name logos for the various Traditions and Conventions? By that, I mean the look of the Tradition(or convention) title? I've just about finished making all the borders, and for the Technocracy, I just used the ones from my current Mage Revised sheets, but I wasn't sure if they did something different in the M20 sheet.<br /> <br /> Anyone want to shed on light on it for me? if they changed them up, any kind soul out there willing to send me updated graphics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T00:51:03-08:00","id":841772,"title":"","content":"They are the same for the Traditions and the Hollowers, all the Crafts got their own stylings for the first time in M20. You don't have M20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:27:22-08:00","id":841780,"title":"","content":"Same look, although FYI they introduced some alternative Tradition names- so if you do versions with alternate Trad-specific sphere names you might consider using them?<br /> The Akashayana<br /> The Celestial Chorus<br /> The Chakravanti (Euthanatos)<br /> The Kha\u2019vadi (Dreamspeakers)<br /> The Order of Hermes<br /> The Mercurial Elite (Virtual Adepts)<br /> The Sahajiya (Cult of Ecstasy)<br /> The Society of Ether<br /> The Verbenae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:33:02-08:00","id":841783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbelith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/525666-m20-character-sheets?p=841780#post841780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same look, although FYI they introduced some alternative Tradition names- so if you do versions with alternate Trad-specific sphere names you might consider using them?<br /> The Akashayana<br /> The Celestial Chorus<br /> The Chakravanti (Euthanatos)<br /> The Kha\u2019vadi (Dreamspeakers)<br /> The Order of Hermes<br /> The Mercurial Elite (Virtual Adepts)<br /> The Sahajiya (Cult of Ecstasy)<br /> The Society of Ether<br /> The Verbenae</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but there are no fonts for those. The Type for the old Trads is available in a set of White Wolf specific fonts and graphics that they published years ago, so it's easy to use the logos and elements on the sheets, the new names are just an afterthought without much impact on the visual design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:35:10-08:00","id":841784,"title":"","content":"Yes- I was thinking as a strapline or subheading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:28:48-08:00","id":841817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/525666-m20-character-sheets?p=841772#post841772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are the same for the Traditions and the Hollowers, all the Crafts got their own stylings for the first time in M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats cool about the crafts. I think I'd only done a couple before...<br /> <br /> <br /> If someone wants to send me the logos, I'll see what I can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/525666-m20-character-sheets?p=841772#post841772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have M20?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not, no.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbelith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/525666-m20-character-sheets?p=841780#post841780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same look, although FYI they introduced some alternative Tradition names- so if you do versions with alternate Trad-specific sphere names you might consider using them?<br /> The Akashayana<br /> The Celestial Chorus<br /> The Chakravanti (Euthanatos)<br /> The Kha\u2019vadi (Dreamspeakers)<br /> The Order of Hermes<br /> The Mercurial Elite (Virtual Adepts)<br /> The Sahajiya (Cult of Ecstasy)<br /> The Society of Ether<br /> The Verbenae</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... Thanks for the info. We'll see how it goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/525666-m20-character-sheets?p=841783#post841783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but there are no fonts for those. The Type for the old Trads is available in a set of White Wolf specific fonts and graphics that they published years ago, so it's easy to use the logos and elements on the sheets, the new names are just an afterthought without much impact on the visual design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to know I can use the logos from the old sheets. Make things a bit easier. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And if I go with the alternate names, I can always make logos using the fonts used for the original name... But, I'm just going to start with the originals and see how long it takes me to get things done.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T18:06:38-08:00","id":842813,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone, I think the M20 sheets are ready! At least the first big round. It's possible there might be a few I missed or a few more to follow..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/m20.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/img/logo-main.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/m20.html\" target=\"_blank\"> MrGone's Character Sheets. </a> 